cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "US Lottery Tax Data: Powerball & Mega Millions Take-Home by Country of Residence"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "ChamTax"
    website: "https://chamtax.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/semilee123456-ui/us-lottery-tax-data"
url: "https://chamtax.com"
abstract: >-
  How much of a US Powerball or Mega Millions jackpot a non-US winner
  actually keeps after tax, broken down by 42 countries of tax residence.
  Each row combines the flat 30% US federal withholding on nonresident
  aliens (IRC 871(a)) with that country's own tax treatment of the
  winnings (including any Foreign Tax Credit offset), computed by the
  same calculation engine that powers the interactive calculator at
  chamtax.com. Confidence levels (verified / approximate / unverified
  estimate) are included per row.
keywords:
  - lottery
  - taxation
  - powerball
  - mega-millions
  - open-data
  - personal-finance
license: CC0-1.0
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-08-21"
